 and β-ribbon connector. The contact surface area is 1277 Å^2 for the 5M16 Fab fragment.","assertion_origin":"source","source_url":"https://www.iedb.org/database_export_v3.php","record_url":"http://www.iedb.org/assay/2546043","link_scope":"record","measurements":[],"target_external_id":"http://www.uniprot.org/uniprot/P0DOK1","assay_ids":["2546043"],"receptor_group_id":"762","id":"ix_f6a2d0e4a676cbc62e6d","target_id":"target:frameshifted-structural-polyprotein-68badd59e658","target_name":"Frameshifted structural polyprotein"},{"antibody_id":"ab_e822d49777c107169418","target_raw":"Frameshifted structural polyprotein","relationship":"binds","evidence":"CURATED","source":"iedb","source_record_id":"762","reference":"http://www.iedb.org/reference/1029588","epitope":"N7, V8, K10, A11, R13, K57, T58, D59, D60, S61, D63, K66, H73, M74, P75, A76, D77, V169, M171, N193, G194, Q195, V229, N231, H232, K233, K234, W235, G253","assay":"flow cytometry · qualitative binding","note":"The most important residues on E2 within the epitope-specific 5M16 Fab binding footprint, were determined by loss of antibody reactivity to 910 CHIKV E1-E2 alanine mutations throughout this glycoprotein. Immune reactivity was assessed using high-throughput flow cytometry. Single mutation D60A, D77, N193A, K234A, or G253A resulted in >50% loss of Fab reactivity, consistent with the cryo-EM results, however, no single alanine mutation on E2 abolished the binding of 5M16.","assertion_origin":"source","source_url":"https://www.iedb.org/database_export_v3.php","record_url":"http://www.iedb.org/assay/2546049","link_scope":"record","measurements":[],"target_external_id":"http://www.uniprot.org/uniprot/P0DOK1","assay_ids":["2546049"],"receptor_group_id":"762","id":"ix_313a4a207afafa363f6d","target_id":"target:frameshifted-structural-polyprotein-68badd59e658","target_name":"Frameshifted structural polyprotein"}]},{"antibody":{"id":"ab_cfdf249785ef5e56a526","name":"AZJ56142_AZJ56143","aliases":["5BQ7_A_B","5F10","AYF64764_AYF64765","UOS91613_UOS91614","WFL44539_WFL44540"],"organism":"Unknown.","format":"paired antibody","has_heavy":true,"has_light":true,"heavy_length":118,"light_length":112,"structures":[],"structure_tiers":{},"exact_structures":[],"homologous_structures":[],"therapeutic_status":"","sequence_quality":{"pairing":"paired","heavy_length":118,"light_length":112,"explicit_vhh":false,"ambiguous_residues":[],"source_format_quarantined":false,"completeness":"unknown_not_inferred","source_nucleotide_available":false},"shard":"cf"},"relationships":["binds"],"evidence":["CURATED"],"sources":["iedb"],"interactions":[{"antibody_id":"ab_cfdf249785ef5e56a526","target_raw":"Frameshifted structural polyprotein","relationship":"binds","evidence":"CURATED","source":"iedb","source_record_id":"759","reference":"http://www.iedb.org/reference/1029585","epitope":"K200, G204, G205, S206, E208, K215, V216, I217, N218, N219","assay":"electron microscopy · 3D structure","note":"The epitope of 5F10 Fab on the Chikungunya virus E2 protein was determined from the cryo-EM structure of the complex of CHIK-VLPs with the Fab fragments at 17 Å to 18 Å resolution. The 5F10 Fab molecules were bound to the edge of the spikes and are oriented tangentially to the virus’ surface and away from the receptor attachment site. This orientation gives rise to numerous steric clashes between Fabs bound to the i3 spikes and Fabs bound to the q3 spikes as well as clashes between Fabs bound to the q3 spikes around the pentameric vertices. Thus not all of the symmetry related sites can be occupied. Escape mutation V216E  was previously identified and lies within the 5F10 Fab footprint on E2.","assertion_origin":"source","source_url":"https://www.iedb.org/database_export_v3.php","record_url":"http://www.iedb.org/assay/2546064","link_scope":"record","measurements":[],"target_external_id":"http://www.uniprot.org/uniprot/P0DOK1","assay_ids":["2546064"],"receptor_group_id":"759","id":"ix_c9040a1b499c75d28b07","targe